    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "txorphanage: account memory usage instead of weight",
    "user": {
      "login": "brunoerg",
      "id": 19480819,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDgwODE5",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19480819?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/brunoerg",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/brunoerg/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "The orphanage limits the \"usage\" of the orphans it stores, per peer and\r\nglobally, to bound the amount of memory an attacker can make us hold on\r\nto. Weight was used as a proxy for that memory, on the assumption that it\r\nis \"often higher than the actual memory usage of the transaction\".\r\n\r\nThat assumption does not hold. Every witness stack element is an\r\nindividually heap-allocated vector, costing its 24-byte slot in the stack\r\nvector plus a 32-byte minimum allocation, while only weighing 2WU. A\r\ntransaction of 199,000 1-byte witness elements weighs 398,247WU (i.e. it\r\nis a standard weight, and witness standardness cannot be checked while\r\nthe inputs are missing), but uses 11.1MB of memory: 28 times what is\r\naccounted for it.\r\n\r\nAccount the memory the transaction actually uses instead, and derive the\r\nper-peer reservation from the largest orphan we are willing to store, so\r\nthat a peer relaying one maximally-sized orphan still stays within its\r\nallowance (and therefore cannot cause any evictions). Orphans that would\r\nnot fit in that allowance are now refused by AddTx() rather than stored\r\nand immediately evicted again by LimitOrphans(), which would first push\r\nout the announcer's other orphans: with weight accounting, a peer that\r\nhad 10 normal orphans and relayed one maximally-sized one kept 9 of them;\r\naccounting memory without the new limit would leave it with none.",
